package api

import (
	"net/http"
)

var _ = declareRoute(routeDecl{
	Method:      http.MethodPost,
	Pattern:     "/api/v1/issues/{key}/nodes/{id}/state",
	Auth:        authAny,
	Description: "Write the node state of the node {id} names {state}: proposed, overtaken or live on any node the store holds that is not gone but the block of an :::ask block of a document, and gone only on a node that belongs to no document - a lens, a finding, a risk or a constraint - since a document's own write removes its block. gone is final: any write on a gone node is 409 NODE_GONE, naming the node. The write that takes a lens, a finding, a risk or a constraint to gone takes its whole part_of subtree to gone in the same write, at every depth and whatever each node's kind - a finding or a risk under a lens, a lens invoked on a lens, a finding, a risk or a constraint, and all that stands under each - those the caller may not see included, so no read by its own address answers one of them once the node above it is gone. A block of an ask, a comment or a message is no node the store holds: every read answers it live, and every value on it is 409 NODE_STATE_NOT_WRITABLE, saying so. A write on the block of an :::ask block of a document is 409 ASK_HOLDS_STATE and writes nothing, naming the ask whose node holds the question's state (the block's own ask or the source ask for a copy) by its dispatch://<KEY>/ask/<uuid> address, or saying no ask holds the question yet. A caller who holds no person scope that sets a person's decision - an answered ask's own node, or a decision a person decided - overtaken or live is 409 ANSWERED_ASK_KEPT, quoting the ask's question or the decision's words and naming the node; on an answered ask's own node proposed is refused too, before the settle's caller rule; nothing is stored. {id} is the node's store address under the issue (`<ref_key>#<block id>` for a block of a document, `lens/<uuid>`, or its whole dispatch:// address), percent-encoded as one path segment; a node the caller may not see under the issue is 404 NOT_FOUND, gone or not. The value is checked first: a word that is none of live, gone, proposed, settled and overtaken is 400 INVALID_ATTRIBUTE_VALUE, naming the attribute state and the word, and nothing is stored. settled is 409 NODE_STATE_NOT_WRITABLE, since POST /api/v1/issues/{key}/nodes/{id}/settle alone settles a proposed node, and so is gone on a block of a document or an issue, a document, an ask, a comment or a message, each naming the node's kind, its state and the value asked for. A move of a lens, a finding, a risk or a constraint into gone is a person's alone - a browser's cookie, or a token holding the person scope - since it takes what the caller may not see: any other caller, the node's own author included, is 403 STATE_NOT_PERMITTED naming the node, in the same words whatever stands under it, and an agent marks a node it wrote overtaken instead. Any other move of a node into or out of proposed or settled, other than the settle itself, takes the settle's caller rule: a person makes it on any node, and any other caller only on a node whose recorded author is the author its credential proves, by the one author rule the settle reads; any other is 403 STATE_NOT_PERMITTED, naming the node, and nothing is stored, so the deployment's shared agent token makes no such move. A move out of settled undoes a decision, a move out of proposed ends a proposal and counts a proposed check or plan task as serving its requirement, and a move into proposed takes a requirement's gaps out of the coverage read and the approval request. On an issue Legion runs, a write of the state of a requirement, criterion or check block by a session that is no person and no architect of the issue or of an issue above it is then 403 DOCUMENT_WRITER_NOT_ARCHITECT, and nothing is stored. The write appends one state tuple on each node it moves, written by the caller - a person's as the person it acts for, as the settle's is - and no event, and every read of the node answers the new state at once; a write of the state the node holds appends nothing and takes no caller rule, since it moves nothing. Where the write changes a query of a converted issue, the issue's queries are marked owed in the write and their versions written once it has committed. Answers 200 {node: {address, kind, state, visibility}, previous}, previous the state it held before.",
	Handler:     (*server).writeNodeStateRoute,
	WriteClass:  scopeProject,
	ID:          &idRoute{Reason: "a node's store address under the issue, which FindNodeUnderIssue decodes and no prefix shortens"},
	// The node state (node_state.go): one write of a node's state, the settle of a proposed node,
	// whose body is an actor alone and may be empty, and the proposed nodes of an issue, each a
	// graph node with its excerpt.
	Shape: routeShape{
		Status: http.StatusOK, Response: nodeStateWritten{}, Request: nodeStateInput{},
	},
})
